  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "CPYTHON-POSTSPAWN-ERROR-OWNER-03",
      "priority": 1,
      "file": "cpython_universal2_stages.py",
      "detail": "run generic BaseException after Popen re-raises raw exceptions; finally fsync/close/result-write may mask StageUnknown. CLI only retains and observes exc.process when exception is StageUnknown, so actual original Popen can be dropped while command/group remains active. Require all postspawn failures to carry the same process/token/result, accumulate diagnostics and preserve original error/UNKNOWN, independent per-fd cleanup; fallback durable evidence failure must never suppress capability. Do not fabricate terminal evidence or remove active guard."
    },
    {
      "id": "CPYTHON-FAST-UTILITY-BIRTH-RACE-03",
      "priority": 2,
      "file": "cpython_universal2_stages.py",
      "detail": "headers runs /usr/bin/lipo and /usr/bin/otool through mandatory live group/birth observation. Those utilities may exit before getpgid/ps, intentionally producing UNKNOWN and fencing otherwise valid headers. Strict byte Mach-O parser already proves architectures/minOS. Remove redundant lipo/otool subprocesses from required path, retaining actual compiler output and byte parser; do not weaken ownership checks for meaningful child commands."
    }
  ],
